## §2 — Comparison with Nagios

Exotel previously used **Nagios** for node-level monitoring. Migration to Prometheus is largely complete.

| Aspect | Nagios | Prometheus |
|--------|--------|-----------|
| **Architecture** | **Push-based** — agents push check results to server. | **Pull-based** — server scrapes targets. |
| **Focus** | **Checks** (up/down, threshold alerts). | **Metrics** (time-series data + flexible querying). |
| **Node config** | Needs NRPE agent + check definitions on each node. | **Minimal** — just install exporter, no complex config on the node. |
| **Querying** | Limited — mostly predefined checks. | **PromQL** — powerful aggregations, joins, rates, histograms. |
| **Dashboards** | Nagios UI (dated). | **Grafana** integration — rich, interactive dashboards. |
| **Alerting** | Built-in but rigid. | **Alertmanager** — flexible routing, grouping, silencing, auto-resolve. |
| **Scalability** | Harder to scale horizontally. | Scales well; separate instances per stamp/cluster if needed. |

**Why Prometheus won:** Near-zero node-side config (just install exporters + tag the AWS instance), better querying, and Grafana integration.

