## §7 — Useful PromQL queries

Prometheus dashboard has **autocomplete** for queries. The API also exposes metrics programmatically.

### Node-level (node_exporter)

**ILL utilization on specific interface in a region:**

```promql
sum(rate(node_network_transmit_bytes_total{group="telephone-server", device="eno5", instance=~"040.*"}[5m]))
```

**Average CPU utilization across cores:**

```promql
100 - (avg by (instance) (rate(node_cpu_seconds_total{group="telephone-server", instance=~"${region}.*", mode="idle"}[5m])) * 100)
```

**Load average (5 min):**

```promql
load5{group="telephone-server", instance=~"$region.*"}
```

### Process-level (process_exporter)

**Process restarts (in last 5 min):**

```promql
changes(namedprocess_namegroup_oldest_start_time_seconds{group="telephone-server", instance=~"${region}.*"}[5m])
```

**File descriptors per process:**

```promql
namedprocess_namegroup_open_filedesc{group="telephone-server", instance=~"${region}.*"}
```

**Top 3 processes by CPU:**

```promql
topk(3, sum(rate(namedprocess_namegroup_cpu_seconds_total{group="telephone-server", instance=~"$region.*"}[5m])) by (instance, groupname))
```

### General patterns

**Rate of counter over time (per-second):**

```promql
rate(metric_name_total{label="value"}[5m])
```

**Increase (total count change over window):**

```promql
increase(metric_name_total{label="value"}[1h])
```

**Percentile from histogram:**

```promql
histogram_quantile(0.99, sum(rate(http_request_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])) by (le))
```

**Alert condition example (high CPU for 5 min):**

```promql
100 - (avg by (instance) (rate(node_cpu_seconds_total{mode="idle"}[5m])) * 100) > 85
```

