## §12 — How each metric type gets set up end-to-end

| What you monitor | Exporter | Port | AWS tag value | Threshold file in getafix | Key metrics |
|-----------------|----------|------|---------------|--------------------------|-------------|
| **Node health** | node_exporter | 9100 | `node_exporter` | `vars/{stamp}/node/default_threshold.yml` | `node_cpu_seconds_total`, `node_filesystem_avail_bytes`, `node_memory_MemAvailable_bytes` |
| **Process health** | process_exporter | 9256 | `process_exporter` | `vars/{stamp}/process/default_threshold.yml` | `namedprocess_namegroup_num_procs`, `namedprocess_namegroup_cpu_seconds_total` |
| **MySQL** | mysqld_exporter | 9104 | `mysql_exporter` | `vars/{stamp}/mysql/default_threshold.yml` | `mysql_slave_status_seconds_behind_master`, `mysql_global_status_connections` |
| **Aerospike** | aerospike_exporter | 9145 | `aerospike_exporter` | `vars/{stamp}/aerospike/default_threshold.yml` | namespace memory/disk usage |
| **Kafka** | kafka_exporter | 9308 | static / ServiceMonitor | varies | `kafka_consumergroup_lag`, `kafka_brokers` |
| **RTPengine** | rtpengine_exporter | varies | `rtpengine_exporter` | custom | `rtpengine_active_dialogs` |
| **CDR** | cdr_exporter | varies | `cdr_exporter` | custom | IP leg record counts |
| **Endpoint** | blackbox_exporter | 9115 | static | custom | `probe_success`, `probe_ssl_earliest_cert_expiry` |
| **Redis** | redis_exporter | 9121 | static / ServiceMonitor | custom | `redis_memory_used_bytes`, `redis_connected_slaves` |
| **K8s objects** | kube-state-metrics | 8080 | (built into kube-prometheus-stack) | Helm values | `kube_pod_container_status_restarts_total`, `kube_node_status_condition` |

### The setup chain (same for every metric)

```
1. Install exporter (binary on VM / DaemonSet on K8s)
2. Tag AWS instance with prom_exporters (or create ServiceMonitor on K8s)
3. Prometheus discovers via EC2 SD + relabel (or Operator)
4. Prometheus scrapes /metrics on the exporter port
5. Alert rule threshold in getafix vars/{stamp}/{exporter}/default_threshold.yml
6. Jinja2 template generates the rule YAML
7. Ansible deploys to /prometheus/config/ and reloads
8. Alert fires -> Alertmanager routes by meta_team -> VictorOps -> on-call
9. Engineer opens Grafana dashboard filtered by group/instance
10. Fix -> metric recovers -> alert auto-resolves
```

