## §14 — Key concepts summary

| Concept | What it means |
|---------|---------------|
| **Scrape** | Prometheus HTTP-GETs `/metrics` from a target at regular intervals. |
| **Target** | An endpoint Prometheus scrapes (IP:port of an exporter). |
| **Exporter** | A process exposing metrics in Prometheus format on HTTP. |
| **Counter** | Monotonic metric (only goes up). Always use `rate()`. |
| **Gauge** | Point-in-time value (goes up and down). Use directly. |
| **`for` duration** | How long a condition must be true before alert fires. Short = flappy. Long = slow. |
| **`group_by`** | How Alertmanager groups related alerts into one notification. |
| **Inhibition** | Suppress lower-severity alerts when higher-severity fires for same target. |
| **Silence** | Temporary mute during known maintenance. |
| **`predict_linear()`** | Predict when a resource will be exhausted. |
| **`absent()`** | Fires when a metric disappears entirely (target gone). |
| **`prom_exporters` tag** | AWS tag for auto-discovery. Comma-separated exporter names. |
| **`group` tag** | AWS tag for Grafana dashboard filtering. |
| **`meta_team` tag** | AWS tag for alert routing to the right team. |

